{:edb/db-before-t 2440 :edb/db-after-t 2441 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535753 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:34:10.186Z" 13194139535753 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364834 13194139535753 true] [17592186292187 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535753 true] [17592186292187 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535753 false] [17592186292221 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069768/assets/b8e6f6b7ab2081595723002737bcb73bbced52bfea0f8cfeb91b1201adab0160.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$" 13194139535753 true] [17592186292221 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/b8e6f6b7ab2081595723002737bcb73bbced52bfea0f8cfeb91b1201adab0160.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$" 13194139535753 false] [17592186364834 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364835 13194139535753 true] [17592186364834 1089 "q-84264" 13194139535753 true] [17592186364834 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535753 true] [17592186364834 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}?$" 13194139535753 true] [17592186364834 1113 #uuid "23106ea0-fa43-51e1-8a52-fa16d0dfecf5" 13194139535753 true] [17592186364834 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =1+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =1+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =1+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =1+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =1+(-0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.$" 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364836 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364837 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364838 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364839 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364840 13194139535753 true] [17592186364835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535753 true] [175921